   "source": [
    "# Diversity in Pottery Form vs. Decoration — first opposite-trend century",
    "",
    "**Question.** *In which century do Diversity in Pottery Decoration and Diversity in Pottery Form show opposite growth trends for the first time, with Pottery Decoration increasing significantly and Pottery Form declining simultaneously?*",
    ""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Authoritative data series",
    "",
    "We use the **raw, non-null century-level Z values** from `data/time_series_data.csv` (`PotteryForm` and `PotteryDecoration`). These 37 anchor points are exactly aligned to ancient centuries and coincide 1-for-1 with `ZKeform` and `Zkeverz` in `data/capital.csv`, which we use as a cross-check. The `_inter` columns are smooth interpolations across 3,600 years from only 37 observed anchors and would manufacture spurious intra-century movements; they are *not* used in the primary decision rule.",
    ""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 · Load data and parse comma-decimal Z columns in `capital.csv`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 1,
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from scipy.stats import theilslopes\n",
    "import math\n",
    "\n",
    "ts = pd.read_csv('data/time_series_data.csv')\n",
    "cap = pd.read_csv('data/capital.csv')\n",
    "\n",
    "# capital.csv stores all Z columns as German-comma-decimal strings\n",
    "for c in cap.columns:\n",
    "    if c not in ('group', 'color') and (cap[c].dtype == object\n",
    "                                        or str(cap[c].dtype).startswith('str')):\n",
    "        cap[c] = pd.to_numeric(\n",
    "            cap[c].astype(str).str.replace(',', '.'), errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('time_series_data.csv shape:', ts.shape,\n",
    "      ' / dtype counts:', dict(ts.dtypes.value_counts()))\n",
    "print('capital.csv         shape:', cap.shape,\n",
    "      ' / dtype counts:', dict(cap.dtypes.value_counts()))\n",
    "print('Non-null raw PotteryForm in time_series      :',\n",
    "      int(ts['PotteryForm'].notna().sum()))\n",
    "print('Non-null raw PotteryDecoration in time_series:',\n",
    "      int(ts['PotteryDecoration'].notna().sum()))\n",
    "print('PotteryForm (ZKeform) in capital (per century)     :',\n",
    "      int(cap['ZKeform'].notna().sum()))\n",
    "print('PotteryDecoration (Zkeverz) in capital (per century):',\n",
    "      int(cap['Zkeverz'].notna().sum()))\n",
    ""
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "time_series_data.csv shape: (3601, 37)  / dtype counts: {dtype('float64'): np.int64(34), dtype('int64'): np.int64(3)}",
      "capital.csv         shape: (39, 15)  / dtype counts: {dtype('float64'): np.int64(12), <StringDtype(storage='python', na_value=nan)>: np.int64(2), dtype('int64'): np.int64(1)}",
      "Non-null raw PotteryForm in time_series      : 37",
      "Non-null raw PotteryDecoration in time_series: 37",
      "PotteryForm (ZKeform) in capital (per century)     : 39",
      "PotteryDecoration (Zkeverz) in capital (per century): 39",
      ""
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 · Take 37 raw anchor rows and cross-check with `capital.csv`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": 2,
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "sub = ts[ts['PotteryForm'].notna() & ts['PotteryDecoration'].notna()].copy()\n",
    "sub = sub[['CE', 'calBP', 'PotteryForm', 'PotteryDecoration']].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "sub['BCE'] = -sub['CE']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort chronologically: oldest first => most-negative CE first\n",
    "sub = sub.sort_values('CE', ascending=True).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cross-check with capital.csv over the overlap window\n",
    "cap_s = cap.sort_values('BCE', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "overlap = cap_s[(cap_s['BCE'] >= sub['BCE'].min())\n",
    "                & (cap_s['BCE'] <= sub['BCE'].max())].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "sub_al = sub[sub['BCE'].isin(overlap['BCE'])].sort_values(\n",
    "    'BCE', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "chk_form = np.allclose(sub_al['PotteryForm'].values, overlap['ZKeform'].values)\n",
    "chk_dec  = np.allclose(sub_al['PotteryDecoration'].values,\n",
    "                       overlap['Zkeverz'].values)\n",
    "print(f'Overlap window : {overlap[\"BCE\"].max()} BCE -> '\n",
    "      f'{overlap[\"BCE\"].min()} BCE ({len(overlap)} centuries)')\n",
    "print(f'  ZKeform   matches raw PotteryForm?       {chk_form}')\n",
    "print(f'  Zkeverz   matches raw PotteryDecoration? {chk_dec}')\n",
    "print('Sub-table preview (oldest first):')\n",
    "print(sub.head().to_string(index=False))\n",
    ""
